<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan grains/oilseeds tender results - May.</title>
<headline>Taiwan grains/oilseeds tender results - May.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan interests in May bought a total of 158,000 tonnes of soybeans, 88,000 tonnes of corn and 113,000 tonnes of wheat at tenders.</p>
<p>Basic information of May soybean/corn tender results:</p>
<p> May Buyer    Tonne  Origin Type Seller     Price   Delivery</p>
<p>  8  MFIG     24,000 U.S.   corn Tradi	$142.2  July 1-15</p>
<p>  8  MFIG     30,000 U.S.   corn Tradi	$.766   July 1-15</p>
<p> 16  T.Sugar  18,000 U.S.   corn Cargill    $.9976  June 1-5</p>
<p> 16  T.Sugar  12,000 U.S.   soy  Cargill    $.11713 June 1-5</p>
<p> 19  MFIG     38,000 Brazil soy  Cargill    N/A     Late June</p>
<p> 19  MFIG     16,000 Brazil corn Cargill    N/A     Late June</p>
<p> 20  BSPA-K   54,000 Brazil soy  LDC	  $.4038  July 1-20</p>
<p> 22  BSPA-T   54,000 Brazil soy  Peavey     $.4038  July 1-20</p>
<p>Note: Prices based on cost-and-freight basis, in US$ per tonne. Delivery periods for U.S. soybean and corn shipments are stated for the U.S. Gulf Mexico (shipments from the Pacific Northwest are 15 days after the Gulf).</p>
<p>Basic information of May wheat tender results:</p>
<p>(Prices based on US$ per tonne)</p>
<p> May  Buyer  Tonne   Origin Type  Seller   Price     Freight</p>
<p> 13   Flour							June 5-25</p>
<p>	Mill   13,600  U.S.   DNS   Mitsui   $198.15   $22.15</p>
<p>	Assoc  10,300  U.S.   HRW   Mitsui   $194.70   $22.15</p>
<p>		  3,100  U.S.    WW   Cargill  $183.39   $22.15</p>
<p> 13   Flour							June 25-15</p>
<p>	Mill   17,200  U.S.   DNS   Mitsui   $197.70   $20.50</p>
<p>	Assoc  10,200  U.S.   HRW   Mitsui   $193.20   $20.50</p>
<p>		  3,600  U.S.    WW   Cargill  $183.69   $20.50</p>
<p>		  3,000  U.S.   Durum Harvest  $223.43   $20.50</p>
<p> 14   Flour							June 15-30</p>
<p>	Mill   10,400  U.S.   DNS   Cargill  $200.14   $22.48</p>
<p>	Assoc  13,400  U.S.   HRW   Cargill  $199.11   $22.48</p>
<p>		  2,200  U.S.    WW   Mitsui   $182.60   $22.48</p>
<p> 14   Flour							July 20-5</p>
<p>	Mill   14,000  U.S.   DNS   Cargill  $198.69   $21.88</p>
<p>	Assoc   9,900  U.S.   HRW   Agrex    $194.60   $21.88</p>
<p>		  2,100  U.S.    WW   Dreyfus  $170.31   $21.88</p>
<p>Wheat tenders comprised Dark Northern Spring (DNS), Hard Red Winter (HRW), White Wheat (WW) and Soft Wheat (SW). Wheat shipments all are slated for delivery from the Pacific Northwest.</p>
<p>-- George Hsu, Taipei newsroom (8862-5080815)</p>
